  "notes": [
    "Revised 17 Oct 2026 from Matt’s 26 Aug 2026 walk-through: MultiPlus aboard (no inverter purchase, rewire line added); Starlink aboard (satellite purchase removed); life raft aboard (purchase removed, recert added); standing rig replacement mandatory in every scenario; no diesel heat in the low plan; canvas line before Mexico. Tender: aluminium-hull RIB + covered outboard in photos; Highfield/Tohatsu vs AB/Nissan still unconfirmed.",
    "Broker listing still live 22 Sep 2026: $379,000 Anacortes, Seattle Yachts / Alex Knudtson, Denison last updated 17 Aug 2026. Seattle Yachts 2856672_1. YachtWorld 10191914. USCG 1219300, name PARAGON, recreational, Active. Hull 34, built 2008, shoal 5.92 ft / 1.80 m, ballast listed 9,982 lb (factory shoal 8,995). Denison header draft 7'9\" is the other factory option — this hull is the shoal.",
    "2024 packet (Yacht Sales West / SoldBoats print, artifacts/Paragon_2024_listing.pdf): listed 24 Apr 2024 at $379k San Diego field / prose says Paradise Village PV heading to SD, Ian Van Tuyl, LLC owned. Print stamps Sold 24 Feb 2025 at $379,000. Current ask is the same number in a new harbor. Three owners: Annapolis original 2008–21 (Cruisers Forum Paragon19, 40k miles) → CA/Mexico ~2021–25 → Anacortes buyer Feb 2025. Equipment list and hours are frozen from the 2024 print.",
    "Negotiated Price $340,000 is a planning target — not an offer. Same-price flip + frozen 530 hrs + unknown rig + varnished teak is the discount case. Survey Deduct left blank until an Anacortes haul. Cash $400,000 is the top of the MN&M all-in ceiling. Commissioning has to come from under the ask. Loan left blank.",
    "Labor = Hire. Matt is not treating this as a two-year owner refit. Survey and sea trial in Anacortes. First working yard is Sidney / Tsehum after the WA 45-day exit (see Purchase_Tax_Timelines_Eden_Paragon_Terratima.docx). DIY is allowed at Van Isle and Canoe Cove with a work order; this file still costs labour as hired.",
    "Sidney 47 ft averages used in this file (Sidney_BC_Yard_Rates_2026.xlsx, Estimator LOA 47, 3 laydays, FX 0.73, GST on, Canoe env on). Survey haul USD: Westport ~$499 / Van Isle ~$748 / Canoe ~$861 → ~$700 used on Due Diligence Haulout. Full stay USD: Westport ~$1,009 / Canoe ~$1,131 / Van Isle ~$1,331. Paint labour Van Isle $125 CAD/hr published. Blended mech/elec CAD $150/hr (~USD $115 with GST). Westport 47 ft half-lift $446.20 may be a table typo vs 46 ft $538.10 — confirm when booking.",
    "Taxes = $0 in this file if Oregon non-residents take her out of Washington inside 45 days and do not park her as a WA liveaboard. WA use tax is ~8.9% if that clock is missed — do not surprise-add it here, and put the 45-day exit on the purchase agreement (delivery Anacortes, first slip Sidney, dated departure). Already USCG documented; no 1.5% sailboat duty on a domestic documented sale.",
    "Delivery $1,500 is Anacortes → Sidney, not a Gulf of Alaska hop. Insurance ~2% first-year domestic-leaning on a ~$340k close; ocean policy will be higher.",
    "Keep and service, do not replace on day one: Victron MultiPlus 12/3000/120 (aboard per Matt 26 Aug 2026 photos, poorly wired: rewire); Starlink (aboard per Matt); Viking RescYou 6-person raft (aboard; label last stamped 05/2018: recert); Hydrovane 2022 + tiller pilot; Rainman 2021; B&G 11/2020; Quantum HydraNet 2019; Rocna 33 kg + extra 100 ft chain + FX-23; 3 electric winches; bow thruster + 24 V bank; Kato davits; Max Prop + PSS 2021; Frigoboat keel-cooler 2024; Lifeline 800 Ah 11/23 until lithium is scheduled; 2023 enclosure; NL genset 244 hrs advertised; Yanmar 4JH4-HTE 110 hp if the meter is real.",
    "Must add or resolve before the 2029 Pacific: standing-rig replacement (required in every plan); MultiPlus rewire; solar well above 525 W; isolation transformer for NZ/AU 230 V 50 Hz; life raft recert; EPIRB recert; canvas before Mexico. Diesel hydronic heat is $0 in the low plan (no PNW winter aboard) and up to $12,000 on the high side. Dual electronic AP (Jefa line) is optional because the Hydrovane is already there — leave that row at $0 if the vane + existing pilot is the plan.",
    "Known listing contradictions to clear on the walk: AB dinghy + 8 hp Nissan vs 2021 Highfield vs new Tohatsu 11/23; 530 vs 770 hours; 7'9\" header vs 5.92 ft keel block; holding tank not on every copy (2024 print 30 gal); factory fuel 104 gal / 395 L — no extra tank on the public list. 104 gal is tight for a 472 nm ocean hop; Paragon is not EDEN's 172 gal boat.",
    "Swing items that decide whether she fits the ceiling: close price, rigger quote, teak substrate under the 2023 varnish, canvas scope, and whether you buy diesel heat + lithium now. Low path (new standing rig at $16k est., teak only recaulk, no heat, keep AGM, skip Jefa, skip OC Tender) lands about $408k at a $340k close, roughly $8k over the $400k cap. High path is a park north of $450k.",
    "Walk her in Anacortes the same trip as Majestic. Ask on camera: hour-meter + engine plate today; standing-rig receipts or a pull; teak thickness / plugs / seams (not just the varnish story); title chain out of the 2024 LLC; any work after Feb 2025; dinghy and outboard as they sit; heat confirmation (no hidden diesel furnace); tank stickers 104 / 211 / 30."
  ]
